# pyron COSMO DISRUPTION on a 2P DUMMY, at close range (14z-74).
# The 1P-vs-CPU rig (71) fires the EX — stock spent, seq 18 — but does NOT
# crash, while the maintainer reports a crash/reset. Two candidate reasons
# this rig controls for:
#   1. the move must CONNECT (or at least spawn its effect at close range);
#      Pyron's EFFECT data is NOT ported yet (deferred by the 14z-74 plan),
#      so an effect spawn is the strongest crash candidate;
#   2. a watchdog RESET is not a 68k exception, so the crash guard can miss
#      it — the runner should also watch for the match state disappearing.
# P1 = Pyron (0x11), P2 = Victor (0x03), 2P mode so the dummy never moves.
# Stocks poked before every attempt (the EX costs one; empty meter = a
# silent downgrade, the DF/ES trap).
#   POKES="1400:ff8782:11;1450:ff8782:11;1500:ff8782:11;1400:ff8b82:03;1450:ff8b82:03;1500:ff8b82:03;3300:ff8509:03;3700:ff8509:03;4100:ff8509:03"
